==English==

===Etymology===
Coined by {{w|Ferdinand von Richthofen}} as {{etyl|de|en}} {{m|de|Rhyolith}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|ῥέω||flow}} + {{m|grc|λίθος||stone}} (modified to {{suffix|en||-lite}}).

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|geology}} An [[igneous]], [[volcanic]] ([[extrusive]]) [[rock]], of [[felsic]] [[composition]], with [[aphanitic]] to [[porphyritic]] texture.

